# Copy the lines you need into .env.local (gitignored) for local overrides,
# or set them as real environment variables in CI. Everything here is
# optional — with no configuration at all the app runs against public
# testnet-10 nodes discovered via the resolver.

# ── VITE_NODE_URL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pin a specific Kaspa node instead of discovering one through the public
# resolver. The pin is probed first; if unreachable the app falls back to
# the resolver, so a stopped dev node costs ~3s at startup, never a broken
# app. Typical use: the local dev chain (see localnet/README.md).
# Mainnet deploys behind the strict CSP must use wss:// (see DEPLOY.md).
#VITE_NODE_URL=ws://localhost:17210

# ── VITE_NETWORK_ID ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which Kaspa network the app plays on. Default: testnet-10.
# Valid values: mainnet | testnet-10 | testnet-11 | devnet | simnet
# Anything else fails the build (validated in vite.config.ts) — a typo here
# would produce an app that can never connect. Share codes embed the
# network id, so both players' deployments must agree on it.
#VITE_NETWORK_ID=testnet-10

# ── VITE_RESET_MARGIN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How far (in DAA score) the chain may sit below the stored high-water mark
# before the app declares "the test network was reset". Default 1000000
# (~28 hours at 10 blocks/s) — far more than any lagging public node, far
# less than a real reset's rewind. Shrink it only on a private local chain,
# where minutes of mining stand in for that day (see localnet/README.md).
#VITE_RESET_MARGIN=1000000
